[[:db/retract 17592186354860 :question/answer-fields 17592186354861] {:db/id "q-104058/singular-ivp-v1/selection/correct-answer" :answer/id #uuid "a0b3dbd0-63f9-594d-94cb-6b783e0bc8a9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No differentiable classical solution exists." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104058/singular-ivp-v1/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc7ecdf4-9edf-52dc-b394-d454fba788f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices [17592186354862 17592186354863 17592186354864 17592186354865 17592186354866 "q-104058/singular-ivp-v1/selection/correct-answer"] :answer-field/correct "q-104058/singular-ivp-v1/selection/correct-answer" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186354860 :question/problem "Determine whether a differentiable classical solution on an open interval containing the initial point exists for the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "A classical solution must be differentiable on an interval containing $x=1$ and satisfy the differential equation at that point. Substituting $x=1$ and $y(1)=1$ gives\n\n$$\\left(\\frac{1}{1\\cdot1}-\\frac11\\right)y'(1)=2,\\qquad 0\\cdot y'(1)=2.$$\n\nThis is impossible for a finite derivative. Therefore no differentiable classical solution exists for the stated initial condition.\n\nFormal separation on nonsingular regions gives\n\n$$(1/y-1)\\,dy=2x\\,dx,\\qquad \\ln|y|-y=x^2+C.$$\n\nRequiring the integrated level set to contain $(1,1)$ yields $C=-2$, hence $\\ln|y|-y=x^2-2$. This is the source's formally integrated relation, but it is not a classical solution of the IVP. Differentiating it at $(1,1)$ again requires $0\\cdot y'(1)=2$. Near $y=1$, continuity would give $y>0$, and $\\ln y-y\\le -1$ makes $x^2\\le1$ necessary on that level set, so it cannot supply a graph on a two-sided neighborhood of $x=1$ either.\n\nThe source capture and its accepted formal relation are retained for provenance. The corrected study answer concerns the original IVP's existence." :question/answer-fields ["q-104058/singular-ivp-v1/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
